# Database Migrations (Alembic)

This directory manages version-controlled database schema migrations for PostgreSQL.

## Structure
- `env.py`: Connects SQLAlchemy declarative models (`backend/app/models/models.py`) to the target PostgreSQL database via `settings.DATABASE_URL`.
- `script.py.mako`: Template used by Alembic when generating new migration scripts.
- `versions/`: Contains all versioned migration files in chronological revision order.

## Commands

```bash
# Apply all pending migrations to latest head
alembic upgrade head

# Inspect current applied revision
alembic current

# Show migration history
alembic history --verbose

# Create a new migration after updating SQLAlchemy models
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe schema change"

# Rollback one migration step
alembic downgrade -1
```

## Applied Revisions
- `cc7e0eccd8d8`: Add `duplicate_of` (indexed self-referencing FK), `UNIQUE(source, source_post_id)`, contact channels (`apply_email`, `apply_phone`, `apply_telegram`), `last_seen_at`, and dedicated `telegram_jobs` / `web_jobs` storage tables for cross-source deduplication and anti-phishing protection.